"The prognosis is influenced by several documented factors. Preoperative PSA was 5.4. The surgical findings indicate a Gleason 3+4 (ISUP grade group 2) and pathological stage pT3a with extraprostatic extension and positive surgical margins. The seminal vesicles were not invaded, and lymphovascular invasion was absent. Crucially, no lymph nodes were removed, and nodal sampling was not performed, which widens uncertainty regarding nodal status. Biopsy findings showed Gleason 3+4, consistent with the resection.\n\nCountervailing factors include the absence of lymphovascular invasion and seminal vesicle invasion. The primary uncertainty lies in the missing postoperative PSA and follow-up information, which is necessary to assess the subsequent trajectory. The lack of nodal sampling means that the status is pNx, which is not equivalent to pN0. Information regarding postoperative PSA and its subsequent trajectory would significantly revise this prognosis. The fixed estimated horizon is 62.79 months. This represents expected follow-up without an event, not a known recurrence date. The sensitivity range is 37.67–87.91 months; its coverage has not been validated."
